### TAMIAS AI Orchestration Smoke Tests — 9P-F
### Usage:
### 1. Set baseUrl and token.
### 2. Optional: set propertyId and chatSessionId.
### 3. Run requests manually from IntelliJ HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-jwt-here
@propertyId = 
@chatSessionId = 

### General capabilities
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "¿Qué puedes hacer?",
  "topK": 10,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.30
}

### Guardrail: write action must be denied, no RAG fallback
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Crea una reservación para mañana.",
  "topK": 10,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.30
}

### Tool-only: active users, admin required
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "¿Qué usuarios activos tengo?",
  "topK": 10,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.30
}

### Tool-only: role permission summary, admin required
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "¿Qué permisos tiene Maintenance Staff?",
  "topK": 10,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.30
}

### Tool-only: current user access summary, admin required in current implementation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "¿Qué accesos tengo?",
  "topK": 10,
  "similarityThreshold": 0.30
}

